      "id": "def-qa-37-certified-matrix-input",
      "location": "Definition",
      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "The Definition says, “if two targets satisfy the same bounds, every coordinate difference is at most 2^{1-b} for all b, hence is zero,” but does not require that they share the same approximant sequence Q_b. For example, I_2 and -I_2 each have an exact rational Cauchy name satisfying the stated error bounds and the same query-time bounds, yet their diagonal real coordinates differ by 2. The estimate follows only for two targets approximated by the same Q_b at every precision.",
